[[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* ½ cup [[Cookbook:Honey|honey]]\n* 2 cups boiling apple [[Cookbook:Cider Vinegar|cider vinegar]]\n* ½ cup [[Cookbook:White Wine|white wine]]\n* 1 pound ice\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Garlic Powder|garlic powder]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] black [[Cookbook:Peppercorn|peppercorns]], cracked\n* [[Cookbook:Dijon Mustard|Dijon mustard]]\n* 1 tbsp smoked [[Cookbook:Paprika|paprika]]\n* 2 tbsp light [[Cookbook:Brown Sugar|brown sugar]]\n* 2 tsp dehydrated lemon peel\n* ¼ cup crushed ginger snap [[Cookbook:Cookie|cookies]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n#Combine salt, honey, vinegar, and wine in a gallon size zip-top bag. Add ice and shake until ice is mostly melted and mixture has cooled down.\n#Add pork loin and refrigerate 2 ½–3 hours.\n#Drain pork and pat dry. Discard remaining brine. Set aside.\n#Combine remaining ingredients except mustard. [[Cookbook:Brush|Brush]] pork with mustard and press spice mixture into all sides of meat.\n#Place roast on a roasting rack in a roasting pan. Insert a probe [[Cookbook:Thermometer|thermometer]] into the center and [[Cookbook:Baking|bake]] at 410°F until internal temperature reaches 140°F for medium rare.\n#Remove to a plate and let rest 10 minutes before [[Cookbook:Carving|carving]]. Serve warm.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using pork]]\n[[Category:Roasted recipes]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Christmas recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using light brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using honey]]\n[[Category:Recipes using dehydrated lemon zest]]\n[[Category:Recipes using Dijon mustard]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Holiday Pork Loin","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 ea. (4 pounds) boneless pork loin roast","sourceText":"1 ea. (4 pounds) boneless pork loin roast","amountText":"1 ea. (4 pounds) boneless pork loin roast","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 cup salt","sourceTe